### Bek-Chat REST API & Webhooks Test File
@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000

### 1. Register User
# @name register
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "dev@bekchat.io",
  "username": "dev_user",
  "password": "Password123!"
}

### 2. Login
# @name login
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "dev@bekchat.io",
  "password": "Password123!"
}

@authToken = {{login.response.body.accessToken}}

### 3. Get Current User Profile
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/users/me
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

### 4. Create API / Bot Token
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/tokens
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "CI/CD Integration Key"
}

### 5. List Workspaces
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/workspaces
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

### 6. Create Incoming Webhook
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/webhooks/incoming
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "channelId": "REPLACE_WITH_CHANNEL_ID",
  "name": "GitHub Deployment Bot"
}

### 7. Test Incoming Slack Webhook
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/webhooks/incoming/REPLACE_WITH_WEBHOOK_TOKEN
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "text": "🚀 *Deployment Successful*: Version 1.0.0 is live!",
  "username": "DeployBot",
  "icon_url": "https://api.dicebear.com/7.x/bottts/svg?seed=DeployBot"
}

### 8. Send Message via Bot API
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/bot/sendMessage
X-Bot-Token: REPLACE_WITH_API_TOKEN
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "channel_id": "REPLACE_WITH_CHANNEL_ID",
  "text": "Hello from Bek-Chat Bot API!"
}

### 9. Get Bot Updates
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/bot/getUpdates
X-Bot-Token: REPLACE_WITH_API_TOKEN
